 # Sessions
 
+Maintainers use this page to understand login lifetime and storage limits when changing request handling.
+Sessions keep members logged in while they assemble a pantry order.
+
 ## Lifetime
 
 Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
@@ -9,8 +12,17 @@ minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Session storage follows [keep sessions in process memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md).
+Request handlers use the shared `sessions` instance in [session_store.py](../../larder/session_store.py).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Sessions are independent in each web process. Run a single web process, or use sticky routing to keep a member
+  on the same process.
+- Restarts and deploys discard sessions; existing Postgres sessions are not migrated. Members must log in again
+  and may need to rebuild the pantry order they were assembling. Schedule restarts outside opening hours to reduce
+  disruption.
 
 ## Shaped by
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- [Keep sessions in process memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md)
